# Creatures and monsters

The woodland, buried ruins and distant mountain keeps around the guild's city shelter creatures dangerous enough to draw the Delvers' attention.[^scope]

| Creature | Nature and place in the world |
| --- | --- |
| Ancient mummified elves of the triangle-gate catacombs | **Several fight the Delvers in [S3E06](../episodes/S3E06.md)** after rune-tombs spiral open; bodies ancient, surgically hollowed, **Krandal Turns Undead but does not instantly destroy them**. Multiple killed and party retreats; exact total/magic origins require recording/map check |
| Behi(r) of Dungeon C4 | Long many-legged lightning-breathing cavern predator **killed by Krandal's Spiritual Weapon in [S3E04](../episodes/S3E04.md)**. Its attack kills no observed Delver; earlier victim testimony says it squeezes prey and is lightning-immune. Unrelated unidentified sticky ceiling ropes/pale crab-like beings are **not proven part of behir**. |
| [Hook horrors](creatures/hook-horrors.md) | Beaked, hook-armed hunters of the deep tunnels. Wild adults retain their separate fates, while Krandal's hatchling Scroungy becomes a tame farm beast of burden.[^hook-later] |
| [Skeletal bat of Dawnless Dunes](creatures/skeletal-bat-balcony.md) | A giant bat skeleton enclosed by shadowy skin and fitted with a harness. Evelyn draws it away from the pyramid and destroys it in the dunes.[^bat-end] |
| [Gricks](creatures/gricks.md) | Scaled predators with grasping limbs and beaks, encountered around forest sinkhole and trapped dungeon. **S3E09:** some disguise themselves as rocks in wind/grick complex; **Koh actually crit-kills a very large alpha and smaller gricks**, Krandal/Barclay kill others, **at least one ESCAPES**. No proof entire population removed or Koh became literal pack leader. |
| [Noble Hollow roper](creatures/noble-hollow-roper.md) | Great stone-skinned creature beneath petrified hollow; **produces piercers**, killed by Evelyn. **Not proven summoned lake beast**. |
| [Skull Keep's flameskull](creatures/flameskull.md) | Green-burning undead sentinel linked, according to Enzo, to a botched immortality rite; destroyed by Koh and banished by Evelyn's holy water |

Reasoning collectives and communities are routed through [Characters](CHARACTERS.md#reasoning-collectives-and-communities): [All Rat](characters/all-rat.md) has a character account, while the [Minotaur Mesa council](places/minotaur-mesa-bone-crypt.md) retains its community history and [Chad Brad](characters/chad-brad.md) his biography.[^routing]

[World reference](README.md) · [Characters](CHARACTERS.md) · [Places](PLACES.md)

[^scope]: This category primarily covers non-intelligent creatures and animal-like or monstrous behavior, rather than talking, reasoning NPCs. [Veggie Sticks](characters/veggie-sticks.md) and the walking plants remain with the character material; Studwell's apparition remains documented in the [crypt dossier](../episodes/S1E02.md). The grick article draws on S1E01, genuine S1E03 and S1E04 dossiers; [S1E09](../episodes/S1E09.md) provides a separate grick's attempt to eat a piercer and the observed hook horrors, without implying a proven life-cycle or kinship. [S1E12](../episodes/S1E12.md) **shows a roper producing piercers** in one collapsed cavern, confirming a local relationship but not universal reproductive biology, and distinguishes the roper from the hypothetical summoning target. [S1E06](../episodes/S1E06.md) provides the flameskull research, observed final banishment and Enzo's separately attributed ritual testimony; no audio-verified episode or audio research, species-wide intelligence ruling or D&D baseline comparison is claimed. Delvers continuity is independent of The Wastes and Inverse. [Category policy](../../project/WORLD_CREATURES_PLAN.md).

[^routing]: Category routing follows the [shared policy](../../project/WORLD_CREATURES_PLAN.md), not an invented intelligence score. [S3E08](../episodes/S3E08.md) gives All Rat a shared voice and a bargain; [S3E10](../episodes/S3E10.md) gives the minotaur council deliberation and voluntary alliance. [S3E12](../episodes/S3E12.md) observes all ten allies become inert bones after Khalazar's defeat, not restored flesh. Older aboleth/leader predictions remain distinct from that observed ending.
[^hook-later]: [S3E06](../episodes/S3E06.md) hatches the youngling; [S3E08](../episodes/S3E08.md) shows its ribbon, feeding and calls, with one of three wild adults killed and two retreating. It is not yet proved trained then. [S3E12](../episodes/S3E12.md), aftermath and one-year epilogue, later describes Scroungy as a tame farm beast. This is an individual development, not universal taming or a proved family relationship. The subject page's full chronological reconciliation remains the next batch.
[^bat-end]: [S3E11](../episodes/S3E11.md) ends during the diversion; [S3E12](../episodes/S3E12.md), ~00:00–00:19, actually resolves the fight with Evelyn's solo destruction of the bat. The scream banishes her elk rather than killing it permanently. Harness, clicks and green gems do not identify a rider or establish exact senses.
